DQL – Data Query Language - Select:
------------------------------------
-> Retrieve all records from a table:
    SELECT *
    FROM 
    CUSTOMERS;

-> Retrieve only few columns:
    SELECT col1, col2
    FROM
    CUSTOMERS;

-> Where: filter your data using where clause
    SELECT *
    FROM Table
    WHERE Condition;

-> Order by : sort your data
    SELECT * 
    FROM Table
    Order by col_name ASC/DESC;
Note: ASC – Ascending order is by default.

-> Nested Order by: sort data using multiple columns
    SELECT * 
    FROM customers
    ORDER BY country ASC, score DESC;

-> Group By: Aggregate your data (combines rows with same value)
    SELECT 
    Student_name,
    SUM(marks)
    FROM school
    GROUP BY student_name

Note: All columns in the SELECT must be either aggregated or included in Group By

Question: Find total marks of each student and show highest marks on top.
    	SELECT student_name,
    	SUM(marks) as total_marks
    	FROM school
    	GROUP BY student_name
    	ORDER BY total_marks DESC;

HAVING: Filter your data after aggregation
-------------------------------------------
It should be used only with Group By clause.

Note: use WHERE clause before aggregation and use HAVING clause after aggregation (Group By).

Distinct: removes duplicate values
-----------------------------------
SELECT DISTINCT student_name
FROM school;

TOP: limit your data – limit the number of rows returned – it works based on the row numbers
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SELECT TOP 3 * FROM school;

Coding order:
---------------------
    SELECT DISTINCT TOP 3
    Col1, 
    SUM(col2)
    FROM table
    WHERE <condition>
    GROUP BY col1
    HAVING SUM(clo2)>20
    ORDER BY col1 ASC;

Execution order:
-----------------
    1.	FROM
    2.	WHERE
    3.	GROUP BY
    4.	HAVING
    5.	SELECT DISTINCT
    6.	ORDER BY 
    7.	TOP
